## 3. Host-Side Action Handler
Inside the host’s `coop.js` (or a new `hostLogic.js`), add functions that Star Multiplayer SDK calls when a message arrives from a client.

### Block Placement Handler
```javascript
function handleBlockPlaceRequest(message, senderId) {
  // 1. Validate
  if (!isHost) return;
  const player = players[senderId];
  if (!player || !player.isAlive) return;
  
  // Check distance (e.g. 6 units)
  const dist = distance(player.position, 
    new Vector3(message.blockX, message.blockY, message.blockZ));
  if (dist > MAX_PLACE_DISTANCE) return;

  // Check if target block is air / replaceable
  const world = getHostWorld(); // reference to host’s world.js
  const currentBlock = world.getBlock(message.blockX, message.blockY, message.blockZ);
  if (currentBlock && currentBlock.solid) return; // already occupied

  // Check inventory (optional: consume item)
  const playerInv = player.inventory;
  const hotbarSlot = message.placedFromHotbarSlot;
  if (!playerInv.hasItem(message.blockType, 1, hotbarSlot)) return;

  // 2. Apply to host world
  world.setBlock(message.blockX, message.blockY, message.blockZ, message.blockType);
  playerInv.removeItem(message.blockType, 1, hotbarSlot);

  // 3. Broadcast confirmation to all clients (including sender for consistency)
  const confirmMsg = {
    type: MessageType.BLOCK_PLACE_CONFIRM,
    playerId: senderId,
    blockX: message.blockX,
    blockY: message.blockY,
    blockZ: message.blockZ,
    blockType: message.blockType,
    // Optionally send the updated hotbar state
    hotbarSlot: hotbarSlot,
    newHotbarCount: playerInv.getSlotCount(hotbarSlot)
  };
  StarMultiplayer.SendMessageToAll(confirmMsg);
}
```

### Chest Update Handler
Chests are trickier because multiple players could interact. Use a lock/open/close flow:

- Client sends `CHEST_OPEN_REQUEST` (chestId).
- Host checks if the chest is already opened by someone else (optional: deny if locked).
- Host replies with `CHEST_UPDATE` containing the full inventory and marks it as opened.
- When a player moves items (add/remove/swap), client sends a *delta* or the new full inventory as a `CHEST_UPDATE` request to the host.
- Host validates the delta (e.g., checks if the item really was in that slot), applies it, then broadcasts the new inventory to all.

Simpler approach (authoritative host):
- Client never directly modifies the chest. Instead, when a player tries to move an item, the client sends a “move item” request (`CHEST_TRANSFER_REQUEST`).
- Host validates, updates the chest (and the player’s inventory if needed), then sends a single `CHEST_UPDATE` to all, plus a player inventory update to the specific player.

