## 4. Client-Side Reconciliation
When a client receives a `BLOCK_PLACE_CONFIRM`, it should:
- Place the block at the given coordinates (using `world.setBlock`), overriding any local prediction.
- Update the player’s hotbar count if included (to keep inventory synced).

*Optional prediction:* You can let the client optimistically place the block immediately, then correct if the server rejects it. The confirmation message will just be a no-op (or remove the block if refused). Keep it simple – wait for the confirmation to avoid ghost blocks.

In `coop.js`, register the message handler:

```javascript
StarMultiplayer.OnMessageReceived((msg, senderId) => {
  switch(msg.type) {
    case MessageType.BLOCK_PLACE_CONFIRM:
      world.setBlock(msg.blockX, msg.blockY, msg.blockZ, msg.blockType);
      if (msg.playerId === localPlayerId) {
        hotbar.setSlotCount(msg.hotbarSlot, msg.newHotbarCount);
      }
      break;
    // ... other cases
  }
});
```

