## 5. Chest Container Sync
Chest inventories need a shared data structure on the host. In `world.js` (or a new `containerManager.js`), store:

```javascript
// Map of chestId -> array of slot items
this.chestInventories = new Map();
```

When a chest is created (block placed), generate a unique ID (e.g., `"chest_" + x + "_" + y + "_" + z`) and initialise an empty array of 27 slots. When a chunk is loaded on the host, restore chest data from saved file/DB.

For late-joining players, the host must send the current state of all chests. You can batch this in a `WORLD_STATE` message when a player finishes joining.

---

## 6. Persisting Chest State
Host should save chest inventories alongside world chunks. If your world saves use per-chunk data, embed a `containers` object in the chunk save, mapping local block coordinates to inventory data. On world load, populate `chestInventories`.

