## 7. Integration with Existing Modules
- **`coop.js`**: Add message types, host handlers, and client-side dispatchers.
- **`player.js`**: When a player opens a chest, send `CHEST_OPEN_REQUEST`. Listen for `CHEST_UPDATE` to display the UI.
- **`inventory.js` / `ui.js`**: Chest UI must be read-only until the host gives the latest state; movements trigger `CHEST_TRANSFER_REQUEST`.
- **`world.js`**: Expose `getBlock` / `setBlock` methods already. Ensure `setBlock` is used by the network sync path.

Since hotbar is vertically stacked on the right (as noted), chest UI can follow the same procedural brass-panel style, with no static images.

---

## 8. Testing Tips
- Run two clients on the same machine (different browser profiles) with the host on one.
- Place a block, see it appear on the second client.
- Open a chest on one client, move items, watch the other client’s chest UI update.
- Use the Star Multiplayer SDK’s latency simulation if available.

